          <li><a href="/funai-accomodation-guide">Accommodation</a></li>
          <li><a href="/funai-homePage">Admission in FUNAI</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>

      <div class="section-txt">
        <h3 class="text-color">How to Apply for Admission as an International Student at FUNAI?</h3>
        <p>International students can apply for admission to FUNAI by visiting the International Students Portal and submitting the online application form. All required documents must be submitted by the deadline.</p>

        <h3 class="text-color">1. FUNAI International Student Scholarships</h3>
        <p>FUNAI offers a range of scholarships to international students based on academic merit and financial need. Visit the scholarship portal to apply for available awards.</p>

        <h3 class="text-color">2. Visa Requirements for International Students</h3>
        <p>International students must obtain a student visa to study in Nigeria. The visa application requires an admission letter from FUNAI and proof of financial support for the duration of the program.</p>

        <h3 class="text-color">3. Tuition Fees for International Students</h3>
        <p>The tuition fees for international students at FUNAI range between ₦150,000 and ₦300,000, depending on the program and course of study.</p>

        <h3 class="text-color">4. International Students Application Procedure</h3>
        <p>International students must follow the application process on the FUNAI International Students Portal, including document submission and payment of application fees.</p>
      </div>
